# Chroma library, modern Earth: THE SPHERES OF SOCIETY, title moments of seven new sphere titles (letter d). Library
# thread, 2026-10-09, "v22" update stage 4, item 15 (`sph_titles`; chroma-packs/spheres/title-gaps.md, "The 28 new
# titles"). An everyday pair per title of titles.py that only its holder meets (holds:), in the style of
# earth-titles-careers.lib and earth-spheres-first-jobs.lib: the first moment grows from the title's turning point, the
# second is a later stretch of the same role.
# Syntax: header of build.py. Rules: SPEC.md. Every moment carries sphere: <sphere>, every option the face it acts in
# (a cross option X>Y the means colour's face). ladder: is the rung the title sits on in that face's ladder
# (character.jobs, read rung by rung); haunt: where the role is done at a haunt among its regulars.
# Evenness: every one-colour option has chance 75 and every cross option 65, so each colour's mean is the same.
# Pairs (complementary calls; cross cycles s1 4, s2 4, s3 3, s4 3):
#   quality inspector     WU (s1) / BRG (s2)     standards inspector    WB (s3) / URG (s4)
#   market trader         BR (s1) / WUG (s2)     savings-circle member  UG (s3) / WBR (s4)
#   detective             UR (s1) / WBG (s2)     private investigator   UB (s3) / WRG (s4)
#   park ranger           RG (s1) / WUB (s2)
# holds: names the new titles, which are not yet in earth_perks_titles.py (they wait for NEW_TITLES to be merged).
# Safety: the detective's and the investigator's moments keep any violence off the page (thefts, a fraud, a tracing
# request, an insurance watch); no harm to a child.

# ================================================================ quality inspector (prod.U)

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- everyday, calls WU (cycle s1); partner: the line's bonus and the reject bin

== three cracked brackets in the sample
tier: everyday
sphere: prod
ladder: regular
at: employer
rate: 0.5
share: .008
stages: juvenile young_adult adult mature elder
age: 17-70
calls: WU
holds: quality inspector
tone: trouble
life: work
horizon: moment
roles: boss, colleague, mentor
earth: near the end of the night shift you find three cracked brackets in a sample of fifty, and the buyer's lorry leaves at six
times: Most quality inspectors, a few times a year; a failed sample against a shipping deadline is the commonest hard call of the test bench (estimate)
gap: 0.5-1
scene: Near the end of the night shift {N} finds three cracked brackets in a sample of fifty. The whole batch is boxed for the buyer's lorry at six, and {boss} wants it on the lorry.
scene W: The rule on the wall is plain: a failed sample holds the whole batch, whoever is waiting for it.
scene U: The cracks all sit on the same edge. {N} suspects one worn die on press four, and could prove it within the hour.
scene B: Holding the lorry costs the firm the buyer's late fee, and {boss} writes {Ns} review in the spring.
scene R: It is nearly six, {N} is tired, and the whole floor is watching to see what the inspector does.
scene G: {mentor}, the old fitter who trained {N}, always said every part leaves the gate with the town's name on it.
- W | put a hold tag on the batch and log the failed sample | v: conformity, security | sphere: prod.W | chance: 75
- U | measure every part from press four before anyone decides anything | v: achievement | sphere: prod.U | chance: 75
- B | let the lorry go, and pass a quiet warning to the buyer's own checkers | v: security, power | closed: approval: shipping a batch known to fail; backfire: the buyer finds the cracks | mark: hid a wrong | sphere: prod.B | chance: 75
- R | stop press four yourself and call the shift over to look | act: stop press four and call the shift over to look | v: self-direction, stimulation | sphere: prod.R | chance: 75
- G | wake the old setter who knows press four, and ask what it is doing | v: tradition | sphere: prod.G | chance: 75
- W>U | sort the whole batch part by part before six, by the written test | v: conformity, achievement | sphere: prod.W | chance: 65
- U>B | trace the cracks to the worn die, and take the proof to the plant manager yourself | act: trace the cracks to the worn die and take the proof to the plant manager | v: achievement, power | sphere: prod.U | chance: 65
- B>R | ship the good boxes on time, and hold back only the boxes from press four | v: achievement, security | sphere: prod.B | chance: 65
- R>G | sort the batch with the night shift until it is done, and buy them all breakfast | v: benevolence, stimulation | sphere: prod.R | chance: 65
- G>W | ask the old fitters to sign the hold tag with you, so the shift stands together | act: ask the old fitters to sign the hold tag with them, so the shift stands together | v: tradition, conformity | lever: voice | sphere: prod.G | chance: 65
works: The die is changed before the day shift, and the lorry leaves at nine with every part sound.
works: The buyer hears about the hold and asks for {N} by name on the next contract.
fails: {boss} overrules the hold, and the lorry leaves at six with the batch on it.
fails: The sorting takes all morning, the buyer charges the late fee, and the floor blames the inspector.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- everyday, calls BRG (cycle s2); partner: three cracked brackets in the sample

== the line's bonus and the reject bin
tier: everyday
sphere: prod
ladder: regular
at: employer
rate: 0.5
share: .006
stages: juvenile young_adult adult mature elder
age: 17-70
calls: BRG
holds: quality inspector
tone: mixed
life: work, friends
horizon: months
roles: friend, boss, colleague
earth: the line's bonus now rises as rejects fall, and the friends you eat lunch with ask you to go easier on the parts that only just fail
times: Many quality inspectors, once or twice in their years on the bench; bonus schemes tied to reject rates are common on production lines (estimate)
gap: 1-3
scene: The firm now pays the line a bonus when the reject rate falls. At lunch {friend}, who works on the line, asks {N}, half joking, to go easier on the parts that only just fail.
scene W: The limits on the drawing are the same on a bonus week as on any other week.
scene U: Half the borderline rejects come off one gauge, and {N} has thought for weeks that it reads a hair tight.
scene B: A friend on the line is worth having, and the bonus scheme was never {Ns} idea.
scene R: {N} hates being the one the canteen goes quiet for.
scene G: {friend} has two children and a mortgage, and {N} has eaten lunch at that table for years.
- W | keep the limits exactly as the drawing sets them, bonus or no bonus | v: conformity, universalism | sphere: prod.W | chance: 75
- U | check the gauge against the master before judging another borderline part | v: achievement, universalism | sphere: prod.U | chance: 75
- B | pass the near misses this month, and keep the line on your side | act: pass the near misses this month, and keep the line on their side | v: power, security | closed: approval: passing parts outside the limits; backfire: a customer sends them back | mark: gave in to pressure | sphere: prod.B | chance: 75
- R | tell the whole canteen straight that the limits are not yours to bend | act: tell the whole canteen straight that the limits are not theirs to bend | v: self-direction | sphere: prod.R | chance: 75
- G | sit with the line after work and show them which parts fail and why | v: benevolence, tradition | sphere: prod.G | chance: 75
- W>B | ask the manager in writing to take borderline rejects out of the bonus count | v: conformity, power | lever: voice | sphere: prod.W | chance: 65
- U>R | rig a quick test at the press to show the line where the parts go wrong | v: achievement, stimulation | sphere: prod.U | chance: 65
- B>G | strike a deal to count the bonus over the whole site, not one line | v: benevolence, power | sphere: prod.B | chance: 65
- R>W | stand up at the shift meeting and say the scheme makes cheats of honest people | v: universalism, self-direction | lever: voice | sphere: prod.R | chance: 65
- G>U | ask the oldest setter on the line how they kept parts inside the limits before | v: tradition, achievement | sphere: prod.G | chance: 65
works: The gauge is set right, half the borderline rejects pass fairly, and the line's bonus comes in.
works: {friend} laughs about it by the next week, and lunch is as it always was.
fails: The canteen stays cool to {N} for the rest of the month.
fails: A customer sends back a crate of near misses from another shift, and every inspector's work is checked for a month.

# ================================================================ standards inspector (comm.W)

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- everyday, calls WB (cycle s3); partner: the cheap chargers on the Saturday stall

== short weight at the corner butcher's
tier: everyday
sphere: comm
ladder: known
at: council
rate: 0.5
share: .0004
stages: young_adult adult mature elder
age: 21-70
calls: WB
holds: standards inspector
tone: trouble
life: work, community
horizon: week
roles: boss, colleague, parent
earth: a test purchase shows the corner butcher's scale gives short weight, and he has carried half the street on credit through hard winters
times: Most standards inspectors, a few times a year; short weight found on a test purchase is the oldest case of the standards office (estimate)
gap: 0.5-1
scene: {Ns} test purchase is plain: the corner butcher's scale gives short weight, a little on every bag. He has served the street for thirty years and carried half of it on credit through hard winters.
scene W: The rule is the same for a chain store and a corner shop. Every buyer is owed full weight.
scene U: The shortfall is the same on every bag. That looks like a worn spring, not a thumb.
scene B: {boss} wants a prosecution this quarter to show the office earns its budget.
scene R: {N} wants to walk straight in and have it out with him across the counter.
scene G: {parent} bought meat from this man every Saturday for years.
- W | write the notice by the book, as for any shop, and set a retest date | v: conformity, universalism | sphere: comm.W | chance: 75
- U | have the scale tested at the office to see whether it is wear or a fix | v: universalism, achievement | sphere: comm.U | chance: 75
- B | put the case forward for prosecution, and let the figures speak for you | act: put the case forward for prosecution, and let the figures speak for them | v: achievement, power | sphere: comm.B | chance: 75
- R | go in at closing time and tell him to his face what the test found | v: self-direction | sphere: comm.R | chance: 75
- G | have a word as a neighbour first, and give him a week to put it right | v: tradition, benevolence | sphere: comm.G | chance: 75
- W>R | seal the scale on the spot in front of the queue, as the law allows | v: conformity, stimulation | sphere: comm.W | chance: 65
- U>G | show him the test figures, and how a new spring would fix it for good | v: benevolence, universalism | sphere: comm.U | chance: 65
- B>W | offer a formal caution if he signs and buys a new scale | v: security, conformity | sphere: comm.B | chance: 65
- R>U | buy a bag yourself every day this week and weigh each one in the street | act: buy a bag every day this week and weigh each one in the street | v: stimulation, achievement | sphere: comm.R | chance: 65
- G>B | ask the shopkeepers' association to get him a cheap scale from their supplier | v: tradition, power | sphere: comm.G | chance: 65
works: The new scale is in by Friday, and the butcher pins its certificate beside the till.
works: The office closes the case with a caution, and the street hears that its weights were checked.
fails: The butcher takes it as an insult, and half the street stops nodding to {N}.
fails: {boss} calls the case soft, and the next big file goes to {colleague}.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- everyday, calls URG (cycle s4); partner: short weight at the corner butcher's

== the cheap chargers on the Saturday stall
tier: everyday
sphere: comm
haunt: comm.market
ladder: known
at: council
rate: 0.5
share: .0003
stages: young_adult adult mature elder
age: 21-70
calls: URG
holds: standards inspector
tone: mixed
life: work, community
horizon: week
roles: boss, colleague, parent
earth: on the Saturday market a young trader sells cheap phone chargers with no safety mark, and his queue is the longest on the row
times: Most standards inspectors, once or twice a year; unmarked electrical goods on market stalls are a steady part of the office's work (estimate)
gap: 0.5-2
scene: On the Saturday market {N} picks up a phone charger from the busiest stall on the row. It has no safety mark, and the young trader is selling them three for the price of one.
scene W: Unmarked chargers start house fires. The law on them is clear, and it is the same for every stall.
scene U: {N} could open one up at the office and see exactly what is inside.
scene B: Seizing his stock would fill the month's report, and the market's owners would like this stall gone.
scene R: The queue is loud and happy. Half of them would boo the inspector who empties the stall.
scene G: The trader's mother runs the fruit stall three pitches down, and the whole row is watching.
- W | seize the stock by the book, and hand him the written notice | v: conformity, security | sphere: comm.W | chance: 75
- U | take three for testing, and tell him you will be back with the results | act: take three for testing, and tell him they will be back with the results | v: universalism, achievement | sphere: comm.U | chance: 75
- B | let the market's owners know, and leave it to them to close the pitch | v: power, security | sphere: comm.B | chance: 75
- R | stand at the stall and tell the queue what is wrong with the chargers | v: stimulation, universalism | sphere: comm.R | chance: 75
- G | ask his mother to bring him over for a quiet word at her stall | v: tradition, benevolence | sphere: comm.G | chance: 75
- W>G | seize the stock, then help him find a supplier with marked goods | v: conformity, benevolence | sphere: comm.W | chance: 65
- U>W | trace where the chargers came from, and report the supplier instead of the trader | v: universalism | sphere: comm.U | chance: 65
- B>U | let him sell out today, and use him to find the wholesaler behind it | v: power, achievement | sphere: comm.B | chance: 65
- R>B | tell him he can hand them over now or lose his pitch for good | v: power | sphere: comm.R | chance: 65
- G>R | gather the row's stallholders to tell him together that it ends today | v: tradition, stimulation | sphere: comm.G | chance: 65
works: The trader hands over the box himself, and next month he is back on the row with marked stock.
works: The test finds the chargers unsafe, and the supplier's warehouse is shut within the month.
fails: The trader shouts that the inspector is ruining him, and the row turns its back on {N}.
fails: He packs up and sells them online instead, and {N} never finds where they came from.

