life: work, money
horizon: months
roles: rival, partner, elder
earth: a new trader sets up across the row with your stock at half your price, and your regulars hover between the two stalls
times: Most market traders, once or twice in their years on a pitch; a newcomer who undercuts the row is a known trouble of market trading (estimate)
gap: 1-3
scene: A new trader has set up across the row with the same stock as {N}, every price cut in half. {Ns} regulars stand in the aisle, looking from one stall to the other.
scene W: The market has a rule against selling below cost to drive a stall out, if anyone cared to use it.
scene U: {N} has priced that stock for years. Half price is below what the wholesaler charges, so it cannot last.
scene B: {N} has a van full of stock bought on credit, and the payment falls due on Monday.
scene R: {N} feels the old itch to out-shout him, out-price him and out-last him.
scene G: Most of the people in the aisle have bought from {N} for ten years and know {Ns} family by name.
- W | ask the market warden whether selling below cost breaks the pitch rules | v: conformity, security | lever: voice | sphere: comm.W | chance: 75
- U | work out his costs, and wait for him to run out of money | v: achievement, security | sphere: comm.U | chance: 75
- B | buy his whole stock off him cheap and sell it on yourself | act: buy his whole stock off him cheap and sell it on themselves | v: power, achievement | sphere: comm.B | chance: 75
- R | start calling out deals louder and better than he can | v: stimulation, self-direction | sphere: comm.R | chance: 75
- G | thank your regulars by name, and add a little extra to every bag | act: thank their regulars by name, and add a little extra to every bag | v: tradition, benevolence | sphere: comm.G | chance: 75
- W>U | post your prices beside the wholesaler's, so buyers can see where the money goes | act: post their prices beside the wholesaler's, so buyers can see where the money goes | v: universalism, achievement | sphere: comm.W | chance: 65
- U>B | switch to the lines he does not carry, and price them high | v: achievement, power | sphere: comm.U | chance: 65
- B>R | walk over and offer him a deal: split the row between you | act: walk over and offer him a deal to split the row between them | v: power, stimulation | sphere: comm.B | chance: 65
- R>G | throw a Saturday street party at the stall, with music, samples and the regulars' children | v: hedonism, benevolence | sphere: comm.R | chance: 65
- G>W | get the old stallholders to agree fair prices for the whole row together | v: tradition, universalism | sphere: comm.G | chance: 65
works: By the end of the month the new trader is gone, and the regulars are back in front of {Ns} stall.
works: The new trader shakes on a fair split, and both stalls have a good summer.
fails: The takings halve for a month, and the payment on the van's stock is late.
fails: The regulars drift across the aisle one by one, and only the oldest stay.

