- G>U | ask the oldest traders on the row what the circuit did to them | v: tradition, achievement | sphere: comm.G | chance: 65
works: The summer ends with the van paid off and the weekly pitch still {Ns}.
works: {partner} says it was the right choice, and the regulars bring the stall a cake in the autumn.
fails: The fairs are wet all summer, and the takings barely pay for the fuel.
fails: The warden gives the empty pitch away, and {N} is back on the waiting list.

# ================================================================ savings-circle member (comm.G)

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- everyday, calls UG (cycle s3); partner: a newcomer asks to join the circle

== the member who took the pot and stopped paying
tier: everyday
sphere: comm
ladder: regular
rate: 0.5
share: .02
stages: juvenile young_adult adult mature elder
age: 16-95
calls: UG
holds: savings-circle member
tone: trouble
life: money, community
horizon: months
roles: neighbour, elder, friend
earth: in your savings circle a member who took the pot early has missed two payments, and the member whose turn is last wants her out
times: About 2 savings-circle members in 5, once in their years in a circle; a missed month after an early turn is the commonest trouble of rotating savings (estimate)
gap: 1-4
scene: Ten neighbours each put the same sum into the pot every month, and each month one of them takes it all. One member took the pot in the spring and has missed two payments since. The member whose turn comes last wants her out.
scene W: The circle runs on one rule: everyone pays every month until everyone has had a turn.
scene U: {N} has kept the book since the start, and can see exactly how short the last turns will be.
scene B: {Ns} own turn is next month, and the shortfall would come out of it.
scene R: {N} has half a mind to go round to her door tonight and ask what is going on.
scene G: She has paid into this circle for twelve years, and her husband lost his job in the summer.
- W | hold to the rule: she pays what she owes, or she leaves the circle | v: conformity, security | sphere: comm.W | chance: 75
- U | lay the book out at the next meeting, so everyone sees the real shortfall | v: universalism, achievement | sphere: comm.U | chance: 75
- B | ask to move your own turn to this month, before the shortfall reaches it | act: ask to move their own turn to this month, before the shortfall reaches it | v: security, power | sphere: comm.B | chance: 75
- R | go round to her house tonight and ask her straight | v: self-direction, benevolence | sphere: comm.R | chance: 75
- G | ask the circle to carry her for three months, as she once carried others | v: tradition, benevolence | sphere: comm.G | chance: 75
- W>R | call a meeting this week, and settle it face to face before the next turn | v: conformity, stimulation | sphere: comm.W | chance: 65
- U>G | work out a smaller monthly sum she could still manage, and put it to the circle | v: benevolence, universalism | sphere: comm.U | chance: 65
- B>W | ask her to sign a note for what she owes, witnessed by two members | v: security, conformity | sphere: comm.B | chance: 65
- R>U | cover her two payments yourself this month, and work out the rest later | act: cover her two payments this month, and work out the rest later | v: benevolence, self-direction | mark: helped someone in need | sphere: comm.R | chance: 65
- G>B | ask her brother, who has a good job, to stand behind her payments | v: tradition, power | sphere: comm.G | chance: 65
works: She pays what she owes by the winter, and the circle goes on as it always has.
works: The circle agrees a smaller sum for her, and at the end of the round everyone has had a full turn.
fails: Two members leave over it, and the circle ends the year at half its size.
fails: The last turn comes up short, and the member at the end of the line blames {N} for the book.

