earth: the station wants a quick charge for a run of shed break-ins, and the young man everyone names was across town on two of the nights
times: Most detectives, once or twice a year; pressure for a quick charge on a run of small thefts is an everyday trouble of a station's crime desk (estimate)
gap: 0.5-2
scene: A run of shed break-ins along the allotments has the whole ward angry, and {boss} wants a charge this week. Everyone names the same young man from the flats. {Ns} notes put him across town on two of the nights.
scene W: The evidence has to hold for anyone, whoever the street has already decided on.
scene U: The break-ins follow the late bus, not him. {N} can see the shape of it on the map.
