gap: 0.5-2
scene: An insurer pays {N} to watch a man off work with a bad back. On the second morning {N} films him up a ladder, clearing his old mother's gutters, and coming down slowly with his face screwed up.
scene W: The insurer pays for the truth, and the truth is two things at once: he climbed, and it hurt.
scene U: One clip proves nothing about a back. {N} would need a week to know.
scene B: The insurer wants the clip, and the insurer is half of {Ns} work this year.
scene R: {N} feels sick, filming a man in pain for doing his mother a kindness.
scene G: The house is two streets from where {N} grew up, and anyone on that street could be filmed for the same.
