earth: in the driest week of the summer you find a family from your village round a campfire on the heath, where every fire is banned
times: Most park rangers, a few times every dry summer; fires lit under a ban are a ranger's commonest summer trouble (estimate)
gap: 0.5-1
scene: In the driest week of the summer {N} smells smoke on the heath and finds a family round a campfire, cooking on sticks. Every fire in the park is banned, and the father is someone {N} has known since school.
scene W: The ban is posted at every gate, and it binds a village family the same as a coach of visitors.
scene U: The wind is turning. {N} knows how fast this heath went up eleven years ago.
scene B: A fine on a man from the village would be talked about in every pub, and {N} has to live here.
scene R: {N} wants the fire out now, this second, whatever anyone thinks of it.
scene G: The heath is the village's own. His grandparents and {Ns} both grazed sheep on it.
- W | put the fire out and write the fine, as for any visitor | v: conformity, universalism | sphere: prot.W | chance: 75
- U | show them on the map how far the last heath fire ran | v: universalism, security | sphere: prot.U | chance: 75
- B | put it out with them, and let him owe you a quiet favour | act: put it out with them, and let him owe them a quiet favour | v: power, security | sphere: prot.B | chance: 75
- R | kick the fire apart at once and stamp the ashes cold | v: security, stimulation | sphere: prot.R | chance: 75
- G | help them put it out, and remind him what the heath means to both families | v: tradition | sphere: prot.G | chance: 75
- W>U | put out the fire and log the spot, so the morning patrol checks the ground | v: conformity, security | sphere: prot.W | chance: 65
- U>B | let him off the fine if he helps put up the ban notices in the village | v: power, security | sphere: prot.U | chance: 65
- B>R | warn him that next time it is the fine and the papers, and move on fast | v: power, stimulation | sphere: prot.B | chance: 65
- R>G | put the fire out with the children helping, and make a game of the bucket chain | v: benevolence, stimulation | sphere: prot.R | chance: 65
- G>W | ask the village hall to put the ban on its notice board and in its newsletter | v: tradition, conformity | sphere: prot.G | chance: 65
works: The fire is out in minutes, and the father helps {N} soak the ground.
works: By the weekend every family in the village knows the ban, and the heath stays unburned all summer.
fails: The father takes it badly, and the story in the pub is that {N} has forgotten their own village.
fails: A week later another fire is lit on the far side of the heath, and it takes a crew all afternoon to put out.

